frontend/src/generated/api-client/** -diff

# core.autocrlf is true on this estate, which means git would happily rewrite
# LF to CRLF on checkout. Two files must not let it.

# SOPS ciphertext has to arrive byte-identical. A CRLF rewrite appends \r to
# every encrypted value, so decryption fails the MAC check and the file looks
# corrupt. The one thing you must never do at that point is byte-edit the
# encrypted file to "repair" it — the MAC covers the key names too, and editing
# makes it permanently undecryptable. Just don't let git touch it.
#
# This is not theoretical: the same omission corrupted the arthur repo's
# secrets file on checkout during the 2026-07-30 rollout.
secrets/*.enc.env -text

# Shell helpers run under git-bash. CRLF line endings break the shebang and
# produce the classic `\r: command not found`.
*.sh text eol=lf
